The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls every report merged into it one issue: the parser
reads dates month first. Read report by report, the merged queue holds three different problems.
One fix will not close them all.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three problems, three tickets. Fixing the parser leaves the other two open.
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table groups reports by tenant and booking form, not by intake's tag. Intake tags come from
the reporter's browser and disagree with the cause in both directions.

## The three problems

1. **Parser swaps day and month.** The shared parser reads dates month first; every tenant in
   #4471 writes the day first. All channels. Ticket: [https://github.com/SrulyAI/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1](https://github.com/SrulyAI/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1).
2. **booking-v3 hint asks for the month first.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under
   its date field. People type what the hint says and the form reads it day first. Form channel
   at booking-v3 tenants only. The parser fix does not touch it. Ticket: [https://github.com/SrulyAI/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2](https://github.com/SrulyAI/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2).
3. **Dates move by one day.** No swap: the date lands a day early or late, and the same meeting
   shows different days in different cities. Listed in the desk's own notes as a one-day move but
   filed under the parser. Cause not confirmed; it looks like time zones. Ticket: [https://github.com/SrulyAI/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3](https://github.com/SrulyAI/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3).

## Why they were merged

Triage merges on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
The three problems share subject lines ("Wrong day on the invite" turns up in all three), so the
subject rule cannot tell them apart. Only the body, the tenant and the channel can.

## Lessons

- Count reports by cause, not by subject. A big ticket can hide more than one bug.
- Read a sample of bodies before marking a merged ticket known.

